<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Nov 8.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Nov 8.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 11/08/96  11/01/96  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    220.14    218.86    94.67	94.11     95.20</p>
<p>West	    228.88    234.26    86.42	88.45     78.30</p>
<p>Total Canada  449.03    453.12    90.28	91.10     86.30</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 11/08/96: 232.55 bcf, 11/01/96: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 11/08/96: 264.84 bcf, 11/01/96: 264.84 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S. -- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
</text>
